From: omarchy-gentoo overlay team <hello@omarchy.org>
Subject: [PATCH] sddm theme: probe the session name via NameRole, not Qt.DisplayRole

SDDM's SessionModel::data() never implements Qt::DisplayRole (it falls
through to the default branch and returns an empty QVariant), so the
"uwsm" probe below always compared against an empty string, never
matched, and sessionIndex degraded to sessionModel.lastIndex. On a box
that also ships GNOME sessions, the greeter therefore logged the user
into whatever session was used last. The display name lives in NameRole
(Qt::UserRole + 4; enum order verified against sddm v0.21.0 and the
Gentoo snapshot dfa5315fd600760f8f3abddf7fb704202ffb07b3).
--- a/default/sddm/omarchy/Main.qml
+++ b/default/sddm/omarchy/Main.qml
@@ -11,7 +11,11 @@
   property bool loginFailed: false
   property int sessionIndex: {
     for (var i = 0; i < sessionModel.rowCount(); i++) {
-      var name = (sessionModel.data(sessionModel.index(i, 0), Qt.DisplayRole) || "").toString()
+      // SDDM's SessionModel leaves Qt.DisplayRole unimplemented (always
+      // empty); the display name lives in NameRole (Qt::UserRole + 4).
+      // Probing DisplayRole made this loop dead code, and every login
+      // fell back to the last-used session.
+      var name = (sessionModel.data(sessionModel.index(i, 0), Qt.UserRole + 4) || "").toString()
       if (name.indexOf("uwsm") !== -1)
         return i
     }
